PostgreSQL Server Package
=========================

This is the build system for the PostgreSQL Server package. It is not
designed to be run standalone, but as part of the PostgreSQL Installer
build system.

Builds are driven per-platform via GitHub Actions (macOS and Windows
binaries are each built on their own native runner - macOS binaries can
only be built on macOS, Windows binaries on Windows). There is no longer
a central Jenkins/VM-orchestrated build reaching out over SSH/NFS to
remote build machines - that legacy approach has been removed.

Build scripts
-------------

* scripts/osx/

Scripts used to build and package the macOS installer. The key ones:
  - compile.sh - configures, builds and installs PostgreSQL itself
    against the dependency prefix (see server/packages-osx.txt for the
    exact pinned third-party library versions).
  - rewrite-dylib-refs.sh - rewrites the built binaries' dylib load
    paths to be relocatable, so the installer doesn't embed the build
    machine's paths.
  - prepare-staging-directory.sh - assembles the built files into the
    layout the macOS installer packages up.
  - createshortcuts*.sh, install-pgadmin.sh, initcluster.sh,
    preinstall.sh, createuser.sh, runpsql.sh - installer-time scripts
    that run on the end user's machine, not during the build.

* scripts/windows/

Scripts used to build and package the Windows installer. The key ones:
  - meson.bat - sets up PATH/PKG_CONFIG_PATH for the dependency prefixes
    and runs meson setup for PostgreSQL (see server/packages-win64.txt
    for the exact pinned third-party library versions).
  - compile.ps1 - drives the actual build (ninja install) and copies
    the resulting dependency DLLs/libs/headers into the install tree.
  - prepare-staging-directory.sh - assembles the built files into the
    layout the Windows installer packages up.
  - createuser, validateuser, initcluster.ps1, install-pgadmin.bat,
    runpsql.bat - installer-time scripts, not build-time.

* scripts/common/

Scripts shared across platforms - currently loadplLanguages.sh and
plLanguages.config, which drive which PL language interpreters
(Python/Perl/Tcl) get bundled.

* generate-sources.sh

Fetches (or repackages, for a release) the PostgreSQL source tarball
for the version pinned by SOURCE_VERSION, ready for the platform build
scripts above to build against.

Directories
-----------

* i18n/

Installer message catalogs, one file per language (en.lng, es.lng,
fr.lng).

* resources/

Graphics, licenses, and other static resources used by the installer
(e.g. edblogo.png, the various pg-help icons, per-platform license
text files).

* scripts/

Platform-specific and shared build/installer scripts - see "Build
scripts" above.

Files
-----

* installer.xml.in

The BitRock InstallBuilder configuration file. The build pre-processes
this to insert version numbers etc. and produces installer.xml, which
is what actually gets built.

* pgserver.xml.in / stackbuilder.xml.in / commandlinetools.xml.in

Additional BitRock InstallBuilder component definitions for the server,
StackBuilder, and command-line-tools components respectively.

* version.txt

Pins the PostgreSQL major/minor version, package revision, and the
versions of bundled components (languagepack, python, perl, tcl,
pkg-config, stackbuilder) for this build.

* packages-osx.txt / packages-win64.txt

Pin the exact version of every third-party dependency library
PostgreSQL is built against, per platform (openssl, zlib, icu, etc.).

* license.sh

Generates the combined third-party license file shipped with the
installer.
